<title>USA: Oceaneering sees gain from jackup sale.</title>
<headline>Oceaneering sees gain from jackup sale.</headline>
<dateline>HOUSTON 1997-03-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Oceaneering International Inc on Friday said it expected to post a &quot;modest financial gain&quot; in the fourth quarter ending March 31 from the sale of the jackup production unit Ocean Ruler.</p>
<p>The Houston company said it was unable to reach an agreement to add additional oil processing equipment and lease the unit under a dayrate lease to Marathon Oil Co, which instead exercised an option to buy the jackup.</p>
<p>The company did not disclose terms of the sale or the projected gain.</p>
